cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "ICS DFIR Toolkit"
message: "If you use this toolkit or its knowledge base in research or published work, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: DePalma
    given-names: Raymond
repository-code: "https://github.com/depalmar/ics-dfir-toolkit"
abstract: >-
  A sourced DFIR knowledge base for industrial control systems and operational
  technology: controller and OT-host artifact catalog with what normal and
  suspicious look like, industrial protocol operations to detect, visibility
  data sources, threat actors with attribution as reported, ICS malware,
  incident case studies, hardening controls and safety-first response
  playbooks, each record validated against a JSON schema and tied to quoted
  primary sources.
keywords:
  - digital forensics
  - incident response
  - DFIR
  - ICS
  - OT
  - SCADA
  - PLC
  - detection engineering
license: Apache-2.0
date-released: "2026-11-08"
